A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate only when evidence supports the **same underlying cause**
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-triage-by-cause), which supersedes decision 0001):

1. Read the body and record expected versus observed behavior.
2. Look up the tenant's locale, booking form and the report's channel.
3. Compare the cause with the open ticket, checking whether the body's evidence fits the model.
4. Merge only when the evidence supports the same cause; otherwise open or retain a separate ticket.

<Callout>
Subject lines and intake tags are clues. They do not establish that reports need the same fix.
The explorer below models tenant and channel; it cannot settle contradictory report wording.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Keep the report separate and investigate. A missing tenant or unexplained behavior is not proof
of a duplicate. See [the #4471 review](/kb/decisions/0002-triage-by-cause) for the investigation
reports held apart from the parser and form-hint tickets.
